{
  "account": "plur",
  "background": { "color": "#0A0A0A" },
  "slides": [
    {
      "type": "cover",
      "main": ["Neural Signal", ""],
      "sub": "Ed Rush & Optical — when drum and bass went into the machine."
    },
    {
      "type": "body",
      "text": [
        "By 1994, drum and bass had found its warmth.",
        "Good Looking Records. LTJ Bukem.",
        "Jazz chords. Long reverbs.",
        "But not everyone wanted warmth."
      ],
      "sub": "Two worlds were forming."
    },
    {
      "type": "body",
      "text": [
        "1995. A dubplate shop in Islington.",
        "Two strangers.",
        "Ben Settle. Matt Quinn."
      ],
      "sub": ""
    },
    {
      "type": "body",
      "text": [
        "They called it techstep.",
        "Dense. Cold. Precise.",
        "Ed Rush and DJ Trace coined the word in 1996.",
        "Not made for warmth.",
        "Made for pressure."
      ],
      "sub": ""
    },
    {
      "type": "body",
      "text": [
        "Optical had engineered Grooverider's Mysteries of Funk.",
        "He had shaped Goldie's Saturn's Return.",
        "The man inside the machine —",
        "before the machine had a name."
      ],
      "sub": ""
    },
    {
      "type": "body",
      "text": [
        "Their music didn't fit Metalheadz.",
        "Didn't fit Prototype.",
        "So they built their own label.",
        "Virus Recordings. 1998.",
        "Not a brand. A signal."
      ],
      "sub": ""
    },
    {
      "type": "quote",
      "quote": [
        "Neuro — the mind, the signal.",
        "Funk — the body, the groove.",
        "Two things that shouldn't fit.",
        "They made them fit."
      ],
      "note": "Wormhole. November 16, 1998. Five records. One track per side. The first neurofunk album. No one had a word for it yet."
    },
    {
      "type": "cta",
      "text": [
        "Virus went on to release Noisia. Mefjus. The Upbeats.",
        "The signal never stopped.",
        "Some music wants to be felt.",
        "This music wants to be processed."
      ],
      "strobe": "The signal never stopped.",
      "cta": "Save this."
    }
  ]
}
